{'symbol': 'ANSS', 'date': '2022-08-01 09:00:00', 'title': 'NASA-BACKED PROGRAM SELECTS ANSYS SIMULATION TECHNOLOGY TO HELP VALIDATE PIONEERING RESEARCH ON AVIATION SUSTAINABILITY', 'text': "IN A FIVE-YEAR PROJECT, THE UNIVERSITY OF CENTRAL FLORIDA (UCF) WILL IMPLEMENT ANSYS' INDUSTRY-LEADING SIMULATION TO ANALYZE, TEST, AND QUALIFY THE USE OF AMMONIA AS AN ALTERNATE FUEL TO POWER ZERO-CARBON JET ENGINES / KEY HIGHLIGHTS ANSYS' SIMULATION TOOLS WILL ENABLE RESEARCHERS TO VALIDATE THE USE OF LIQUID AMMONIA (NH3) AS AN ALTERNATE, MORE SUSTAINABLE FUEL FOR AIRCRAFT THE COLLABORATION WILL SUPPORT, AND POTENTIALLY SURPASS, THE WORLDWIDE AVIATION INDUSTRY GOAL TO REACH NEAR-ZERO EMISSIONS BY 2050 THE SIMULATION-POWERED RESEARCH IS POISED TO TRANSFORM THE AVIATION INDUSTRY WITH AN ALTERNATIVE FUEL THAT WOULD PRODUCE ZERO-CARBON EMISSIONS PITTSBURGH , AUG. 1, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0ANSYS (NASDAQ: ANSS) WILL SUPPORT RESEARCH LED BY THE UNIVERSITY OF CENTRAL FLORIDA (UCF) AND FUNDED BY A $10 MILLION NASA UNIVERSITY LEADERSHIP INITIATIVE FIVE-YEAR GRANT TO ACCELERATE AVIATION SUSTAINABILITY. THE PROJECT AIMS TO DEVELOP ZERO-CARBON JET ENGINES USING LIQUID AMMONIA (NH3) AS AN ALTERNATE, MORE SUSTAINABLE FUEL FOR AIRCRAFT."}